Dear Guangchuang Yu and co-authors,

I am having an issue using ggtree in a Shiny app. The app was supposed to call msaplot, which I believe calls read.fasta from treeio, which in turn calls"readBStringSet" from Biostrings. Unfortunately, there is an issue loading Biostrings. Here is the relevant output from my Shiny web app log:

Loading required package: Biostrings
2018-10-24T19:54:42.136213+00:00 shinyapps[463434]:   there is no package called ‘Biostrings’
2018-10-24T19:54:42.142083+00:00 shinyapps[463434]:   62: read.fasta
2018-10-24T19:54:42.136956+00:00 shinyapps[463434]: Warning: Error in eval: object 'readBStringSet' not found

Note that when I use a normal ggtree plot this error does not occur. Only with msaplot. I don't see Biostrings listed on the Imports or Depends lists in the treeio package--could this be causing this issue?

Many thanks for your help. I'd love to get this sorted and use the msaplot function in my app.

