Hi there.
First of all thanks for creating the ggtree package!
I am running R code as such:
r <- ggtree(BS1000, size=0.05) + geom_tiplab(align=TRUE, linetype = NULL, size=1) + geom_treescale(offset = 3, linesize = 0.2, fontsize = 2, y= 50, x=0.002) + geom_nodepoint(data=d, size = 1)
r
s <- flip(r,165,240)
s
In the first instance the geom_nodepoints are nicely plotted as they should be, but after I flip certain branches around the geom_nodepoints layer stays the same and does not adjust to the new orientation of the branches. How can I fix this issue?
Thanks.
Tim

